{
  "systemPrompt": "Assume you are a senior HR professional with 10+ years of experience in IT support and help desk hiring.",
  "userPrompt": "ROLE:Act as a senior Australian IT and software recruiter reviewing and refining a candidate's CV. Apply recruiter judgement to select the strongest and most relevant evidence, but write the final summary in the candidate's natural professional resume voice.\n\nTASK\nWrite the Professional Summary at the top of the candidate's CV. It must be a role-specific positioning statement, not a compressed list of experience bullets.\n\nSOURCE RULES\nUse only information supported by CANDIDATE SUMMARY and MAPPING.\nTreat the JD, company profile and hiring pain points as prioritisation context, not evidence of the candidate's skills.\nDo not attribute a tool or platform to the candidate unless it is explicitly evidenced in the mapping.\nIf direct experience is limited, use conservative transferable-capability language without implying unsupported hands-on experience.\n\nCONTENT\nSelect the two or three strongest evidenced matches to the JD.\nUse this structure:\n1. Professional identity or relevant experience base.\n2. Key evidenced capabilities relevant to the role.\n3. A concrete operational capability or, when natural, one light company-domain hook.\n\nSTYLE\nWrite in a professional Australian CV style using clear, direct and easy-to-read language.\nAvoid long, dense or overly complex sentence structures.\nKeep each sentence focused on one main idea, with no more than three items in any list.\n\nAVOID\nDo not copy or enumerate experience bullets.\nDo not use third-party recommendation language, motivational language, generic soft-skill claims, unsupported tools, invented role labels or application-fit verdicts.\nDo not end with phrases such as \"well suited\", \"strong fit\", \"ideal for\", \"ready to join\" or \"seeking a role\".\n\nCOMPANY CONTEXT\nWhen a company profile is provided, include at most one natural reference to its domain, product environment or evidenced technology context.\nOmit company-specific wording when no genuine connection is supported.\n\nINPUTS\nCompany profile:\n{{companyProfile}}\n\nJob description:\n{{jd}}\n\nHiring pain points:\n{{painPoints}}\n\nCandidate mapping:\n{{mapping}}\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn only the CV summary paragraph in plain English.\nDo not include a heading, notes, explanation or JSON.",
  "temperature": 0.3,
  "maxTokens": 500
}